-- title:
--   Horizontal unramifiedness over the Γ₀(M') floor, case q=2
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q=2$, a positive integer $M'$ not divisible by $q$, and a field $L$ of characteristic zero, algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ and admitting a ring embedding into $\mathbb{C}$ carrying $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as `laurentBaseChange`, i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field `xHFunctionField` of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup `levelH q M'` of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ (the kernel of the unit reduction map `ZMod.unitsMap` along `dvd_sq_mul q M'`), and let $K_0 \le K$ be the corresponding base change of the $q$-expansion function field `qExpFunctionFieldC` of $\Gamma_0(M')$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, with uniformiser $\varpi$, and with compatible $A$-algebra structures on $K$ and $K_0$. Let $j \in K$ and $j_0 \in K_0$ be nonzero elements whose Laurent expansions are both the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion `jq` of the modular invariant, and write $A_{\mathrm{fin}}(K) =$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, similarly $A_{\mathrm{fin}}(K_0)$; let $\iota : A_{\mathrm{fin}}(K_0) \to A_{\mathrm{fin}}(K)$ be a ring homomorphism inducing the inclusion $K_0 \le K$, used as the algebra structure in the conclusion. Further data: a valuation subring $W_0$ of $K$ consisting of those $f$ for which there are power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal and $f \cdot \bar y = \bar x$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ (images under $A \to L$); a point $z$ of the two-chart integral model `TwoChartIntegralModel A K j` (the pushout of the two chart spectra) at which the germ $\varpi z$ of the image of $\varpi$ from the base lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk; a point $y$ of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_{\mathrm{fin}}(K)$ with `ιFin`-image $z$ and maximal prime ideal; an algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\varphi : A_{\mathrm{fin}}(K) \to \Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, such that $\varphi(j)$ does not lie in `ssJSet q Ω` (the set of those $j$ for which every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with invariant $j$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$), together with the condition that every element of $A_{\mathrm{fin}}(K)$ which is a nonunit of $W_0$ lies in the prime of $y$. Assume finally $\varphi(j) \neq 0$ and $\varphi(j) \neq 1728$. Then for every prime ideal $\mathfrak{Q}$ of $A_{\mathrm{fin}}(K)$ with $\mathfrak{Q}$ contained in the prime of $y$, of height $1$, and not containing the image of $\varpi$, the algebra $A_{\mathrm{fin}}(K)$ is unramified at $\mathfrak{Q}$ over $A_{\mathrm{fin}}(K_0)$ in the sense of `Algebra.IsUnramifiedAt`.
--
--   This is the horizontal (characteristic-zero fibre) unramifiedness statement for the covering of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-model by the full-level model at $j$-invariants away from $0$ and $1728$, in the case $q=2$; the ramification of the modular covering is concentrated over the elliptic points $j=0,1728$ and the cusps. It feeds the proof that the fibre of the two-chart integral model at an ordinary maximal point with the Gauss-valuation condition is a regular local ring.
